{{!
    @template local_oksigeniaayvurenda/visit
    A room of the library one visits: its painted layers (by day, or by night in dark mode), the places one touches,
    the surfaces where the library writes its own (the board of corners, the stand of new books, the blackboard), the
    characters standing in it, and the same places as a row of words. The script scales the painting to the screen and
    shows it (the layers wait as a blank pixel, so a dark page never loads the day); without the script, the row of words
    is the visit.
    Context variables required for this template:
    * name, title, width, height, focus, depth, sound, door, touch - the room
    * back, front - layers: day, night, depth
    * zones - places: id, url, label, points, tipx, tipy, cy, enters
    * surfaces - each directory (rows: label, url, colour, enters; rowheight), pulse (heading, lines) or book (title, cover,
      colour, url), with width, height, transform, fontsize and ink (the colours the painting asks, as CSS)
    * characters - role, name, text, figure, puppet, size, left, top, depth, search (action, slug), play and playid (the
      herald offers the room's game), voice (the memory's hello)
    * young - a reader of the flower: the sound is on unless they turned it off
    * hunt - the room's game, or nothing: target, heading, name, clue, figure, puppet, cheer, cheerpuppet, huntcover,
      huntlines, huntplace, labelsr, spines, title, found, foundhint, recordurl, againurl, messages, voices
    * sort - the hall's game, or nothing: heading, name, intro, figure, puppet, cheer, cheerpuppet, books (id, title,
      photo, colour, corner, cornerlabel, topic, lines, count, labelsr, url, first), doors (code, label, colour, art),
      againurl, messages, voices; hasplaces
    * visitplaces, visitsound, visitpanleft, visitpanright, visitclose, searchlabel, searchplaceholder, searchbutton
    Example context (json):
